## Scoring Rationale

**Paper summary:** SAM proposes a Transformer-based world model for RL environments with *superposed* (mixture) causal relationships. It uses a score-based variational objective with Gumbel-Softmax to infer trajectory-specific causal masks end-to-end. Experiments on two custom synthetic environments show strong SHD improvements over baselines.

### Dimension-by-Dimension Comparison

| Dimension | Assessment | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| **Novelty** | Moderate-High | Superposed causal relationships in RL is a clearly new and well-motivated problem formulation. The trajectory-level in-context causal inference framing is creative. |
| **Technical soundness** | Moderate | ELBO + Gumbel-Softmax is solid but derivative. Equation error in core definition (conditioning on $s_{t+1}$ instead of $s_t$). Stop-gradient rationale missing. Identifiability entirely unaddressed. |
| **Empirical support** | Weak–Moderate | Only 2 bespoke synthetic environments. No statistical uncertainty (no standard deviations). Missing prediction accuracy for one entire environment (Confusing-Minigrid). Missing critical meta-RL context baselines. Unexplained M012-C012 anomaly. |
| **Significance** | Moderate | If validated more broadly, the problem setting is practically important. As-is, narrow scope limits practical impact. |
| **Clarity** | Moderate | Good high-level motivation; insufficient architecture details for reproducibility; some equation errors. |

### Calibration Comparisons

